{
  "note": "The hero's weapon effects (design.md, The Look > Weapon effects; Render/Effects/Effects.cs reads it). Each cue (EffectCue, camel-cased) is a list of layers drawn from its shot (EffectShot: its time, point, path, facing, reach, arc, span, power). shape: arc (one of Hovl's slash meshes, mesh Slash1-4, round its point, its head sweeping the arc), ribbon (a flat strip along the path, or radius m along the facing), upright (a strip standing radius m tall: a figure's glow), solid (Hovl's MagicSword, radius its length, tilt its pitch) or sparks (a compute burst: count, speed and life [min, max], spread degrees round its way, up, size m, drag 1/s, gravity). at: at (the shot's point, the default), to (its path's end), path (repeats spaced along the path), around (repeats spacing m round the point, each facing out by yaw + i yawStep), edge (sparks: where a slash's sweep ends on its arc). repeat copies each every s later; alternate mirrors every other's sweep; delay is s after the shot's time (negative: before, a sword falling onto its impact). radius (m) and arc (degrees; a ribbon's half width in m): radiusShot times the shot's reach when it gives one (the sim sized it for the beat), arcShot its arc; otherwise the power's scale. Timing in seconds: sweep (the head, fast in and slow out; sweepShot: the shot's span), travel (the move and growth; travelShot: the shot's span; default the sweep), linger after both, and fade (default the linger) at the end, as the noise dissolves it. width is the band's share lit at the head, narrowing to nothing behind it (Hovl's crescent taper); brightness the HDR gain (white core, faint white-blue edge; above 1 blooms); streak the noise streaks' depth; grow the scale at birth (a shockwave racing out); travelPath moves it along the path, travelM along its facing, travelUpM up; taper 0 draws an even band (a ring, a figure). powers: brightness and spark count for every layer, scale for a layer the recipe sizes. orbitBlades and bladeHalo: each sword's layers (a solid, and an arc trailing it radius m outside the ring).",
